{{name}}: deployment files (generated by Build Game, Dedicated server)

  {{slug}}.service        systemd unit, one instance (install.sh puts it in /etc/systemd/system)
  {{slug}}@.service       systemd template unit, several instances: systemctl enable --now {{slug}}@arena1
  server.ron              production settings (state_dir {{state_dir}}, outside the build folder)
  instance.ron.example    settings of one instance of the template unit
  {{slug}}.env.example    secrets (password, relay token): /etc/{{slug}}/{{slug}}.env, mode 0600
  Dockerfile              image from the prebuilt binary (docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .)
  docker-compose.yml      compose file: volume for the state folder, health check, read-only root
  nftables.nft, ufw.sh    firewall examples
  logrotate.conf          /etc/logrotate.d/{{slug}}
  kubernetes.yaml        PVC + Deployment + UDP Service (kubectl apply -f)
  install.sh              user, folders and units on a systemd host (does not start anything)

Ports (UDP): {{game_port}} game, {{admin_port}} signed admin (operators only), 47777 LAN discovery (closed
on a public host), 47800 relay (only if you run one). The ONE folder to keep and back up is
{{state_dir}} (identity.key, bans.ron, world.state*, players.state*).
Health probe: zestengine-server --healthcheck --config <server.ron> (exit 0 alive, 1 not).
Effective settings: zestengine-server --print-config --config <server.ron>
Full guide: docs/deployment/dedicated-server.md in the ZestEngine checkout.
